<BaseLayout
  title="O’Reilly’s table for three hours until Four Corner 14:00 | Dubliners"
  description="Sunday 8 Nov ~11:00: three hours until Four Corner opens. Sit a table at O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar, Pasaje de Matheu 4, then hop Victoria 6 at 14:00 and Espoz y Mina 7. Restaurant-first, Maps, metres. No invented menu."
  path={PATH}
  lang="en"
  hreflang={{ en: PATH, es: PATH_ES }}
  ogImage="/images/dubliners-screens-sol-1200.webp"
  extraJsonLd={[articleLd, faqLd]}
>
  <section class="hero hero-compact" data-show-until={SHOW_UNTIL}>
    <div class="container">
      <Breadcrumb current="Three hours to spare: O’Reilly’s table until Victoria 6 at 14:00" schema />
      <h1>Three hours to spare: sit an O’Reilly’s table, then hop Victoria 6 at 14:00</h1>
      <p class="lead">
        Saturday is over. It is about 11:00. Four Corner on Calle de la Victoria 6 does <strong>not</strong> open before 14:00.
        You have <strong>three hours to spare</strong> — sit down at a <strong>table</strong> at O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar, Pasaje de Matheu 4.
        Restaurant-first. Not a standing pint under glass, not a lunch-then-Bengals itinerary.
        At 14:00 hop to Victoria 6 (sports screens) and to Espoz y Mina 7. We do not invent a menu. Maps below.
      </p>
      <p class="small">En español: <a href={withBase(PATH_ES)} hreflang="es" lang="es">Tres horas libres: mesa en O’Reilly’s, luego salto a Victoria 6 a las 14:00</a></p>
      <FanWeekendCtas lang="en" findHref="/visit/" />
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>A restaurant table until 14:00 — not a glass-arcade pint, not lunch-then-screens</h2>
      <p>
        Other pages already cover a first pint under the Pasaje de Matheu glass roof, Sunday lunch then Dubliners at 15:30,
        and Four Corner’s 14:00 open on its own.
        This page is only the <strong>sit-down table that fills the three hours from ~11:00 until Victoria 6 opens</strong>.
        Ask for a table. We do not list the carta. We do not invent hours beyond what is already usual on this site.
      </p>

      <h2>From ~11:00 — pin the table, then the two hops</h2>
      <p>
        O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar, <strong>Pasaje de Matheu 4</strong>. Usual from 11:30 (already published on this site).
        From about 11:00 that is <strong>about half an hour</strong> until the usual open, then <strong>about two and a half hours</strong>
        at the table until Four Corner 14:00. Pin the passage now. If the door is still shut, wait in the passage — do not camp Victoria 6 before 14:00.
      </p>
      <p>
        Sit the table. Then hop:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>14:00 — around to Victoria 6.</strong>
          Four Corner from 14:00 until late, sports screens, not open before.
          About <strong>2 min / 120–180 m</strong>. That is the door you were waiting for; leave the table for it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Out onto Espoz y Mina 7</strong> — the street the restaurant opens onto.
          Dubliners and O’Connell’s, same number, two doors. About <strong>1 min / 40–80 m</strong>. Both from 12:00 today (O’Connell’s usual Sunday 14:00).
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>After the hop — coordinate, do not substitute</h2>
      <p>
        Named on Dubliners <a href={withBase('/whats-on/')}>What’s On</a> (ask which screen — not every game on every screen):
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>15:00</strong> — Crystal Palace vs Liverpool · Sunderland vs Chelsea · Brighton vs Brentford · Ipswich Town vs Bournemouth</li>
        <li><strong>15:30</strong> — Bengals vs Falcons LIVE (NFL Madrid Game)</li>
        <li><strong>17:30</strong> — Manchester United vs Aston Villa</li>
        <li><strong>from 19:00</strong> — NFL evening / RedZone · <strong>21:00</strong> — Atlético vs Barcelona</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        We do not copy that board onto O’Reilly’s, O’Connell’s or Four Corner. The table is the three-hour sit; the hop is for screens from 12:00 / 14:00.
        Premier, NFL and Atleti sit alongside; coordinate, do not substitute.
      </p>

      <h2>Table, then the hops — addresses</h2>
      <ol>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Reilly’s Restaurant Bar — Pasaje de Matheu 4, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Sit a table from the usual 11:30 until you leave for 14:00. Terrace restaurant-bar. We do not list the carta or invent a Sunday special.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oreillys} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Four Corner — Calle de la Victoria 6, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          Opens 14:00 until late · sports screens. Not open before 14:00. About 2 min from the table. Ask which game is on.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.fourCorner} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Dubliners — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid.</strong>
          ~1 min out of the passage. Sunday from 12:00. Named Premier, NFL and Atleti listings on What’s On. Ask which screen.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.dubliners} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>O’Connell’s — Calle de Espoz y Mina 7, 28012 Madrid</strong> (Maps listing: O’Connell St).
          The other door at the same number, ~1 min from the table. From 12:00 today (usual Sunday 14:00). Meeting point; we do not invent its board.
          {' '}<a href={MAPS.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Maps</a>
          {' · '}<a href={DIR.oconnell} rel="noopener noreferrer" target="_blank">Walking directions</a>.
        </li>
      </ol>

      <OriginalFourBars lang="en" when="sunday" findHref="/visit/" />

      <h2>FAQ</h2>
      <dl class="faq">
        <dt><strong>~11:00, three hours until Four Corner. Where do I sit?</strong></dt>
        <dd>A table at O’Reilly’s, Pasaje de Matheu 4. Usual 11:30. Pin the passage now; wait there, not on Victoria 6. Four Corner from 14:00, sports screens, not before.</dd>
        <dt><strong>How far from the table to Victoria 6 and Espoz y Mina 7?</strong></dt>
        <dd>Number 7 is ~1 min / 40–80 m. Victoria 6 ~2 min / 120–180 m. Leave the table for 14:00. Named listings: Dubliners What’s On only.</dd>
        <dt><strong>Does the table replace Premier, NFL or Atleti 21:00?</strong></dt>
        <dd>No. Coordinate. 15:00 Premier block, United 17:30, NFL 15:30 / from 19:00, Atleti 21:00 sit alongside after you hop. We do not assign a match to O’Reilly’s or Four Corner, and we do not invent a menu.</dd>
      </dl>

